<title>ARGENTINA: Argentine monthly grain/oilseed shipments.</title>
<headline>Argentine monthly grain/oilseed shipments.</headline>
<dateline>BUENOS AIRES 1996-10-02</dateline>
<text>
<p>Agriculture Secretariat July grain shipment figures (tonnes), followed by January-July totals (year-earlier in brackets).</p>
<p> Wheat	212,194  (399,147)     2,916,274  (5,689,705)</p>
<p> Maize    1,019,181  (507,486)     4,878,638  (4,827,769)</p>
<p> Sorghum     28,135   (41,609)	 578,126    (133,012)</p>
<p> Barley	   nil	(nil)	   6,888     (21,400)</p>
<p> Soybeans   254,644  (439,485)     1,729,679  (2,318,638)</p>
<p> Sunseed	1,833   (90,065)	 536,117    (793,224)</p>
<p> Others	46,773   (15,625)	 160,178    (152,538)</p>
<p>Principal destinations in July were as follows (tonnes):</p>
<p>WHEAT: Brazil 207,421; Paraguay 4,658; Germany 115</p>
<p>MAIZE: Colombia 249,491; Egypt 170,123; Iran 124,469; Malaysia 90,840; Syria 52,548; Indonesia 52,660</p>
<p>SOYBEANS; Holland 124,775; Spain 33,300; Chile 32,577; Indonesia 20,392</p>
<p>-- Buenos Aires Newsroom +541 318-0655</p>
</text>
